window.MirchiSearch=[{"title":"Overview · The 60-second business brief","url":"/radio-mirchi#brief","text":" Radio Mirchi is the flagship brand within listed Entertainment Network (India) Limited (ENIL), part of the Times Group. Think of it as a city-centric entertainment and advertiser business with several ways to earn: broadcast advertising, branded solutions, events, digital services and subscriptions. S7 S6 My thesis: the opportunity is to make Mirchi’s local trust, creators and cultural IP convert into repeat advertiser spend and durable consumer relationships. Revenue growth is useful only when contribution, working capital and customer value improve with it. ₹116.70 cr Q2 FY27 consolidated revenue Down 17.3% YoY S1 ₹12.05 cr Q2 FY27 consolidated EBITDA Up 5.9% YoY S1 53% / 29% Radio / digital domestic mix Management’s rounded Q2 shares S2 73 / 63 Indian stations / cities Company-reported footprint S7 "},{"title":"Overview · Three decisions I would put on the table","url":"/radio-mirchi#readout","text":" Core business Protect radio’s value Improve yield and the advertiser’s reason to renew. A discount that fills inventory can still destroy contribution. Build proof around a defined city outcome. Events Scale the right events Choose repeatable formats with committed sponsorship, clear cash exposure and a realistic break-even ticket count. Evaluate each city and edition independently. Digital Make distribution pay back Judge Gaana partnerships by activation, retained listening and renewal contribution. Devices shipped, trials started and social views are intermediate signals. "},{"title":"Overview · Choose your preparation route","url":"/radio-mirchi#paths","text":" Time available Read in this order What to remember 10 minutes Financials , current initiatives , interview The company, the latest numbers, your opening answer. 45 minutes Business, revenue, radio, events, digital, platforms How each business works and where evidence ends. Deep preparation Competition, opportunities, plan, metrics, economics lab, sources Defend prioritisation, quantify a trade-off and ask informed questions. How to read the study “Reported” means a company or primary-source claim. “Observed” means a public page was inspected. “Hypothesis” and “Proposed” are my analysis. A missing public metric is a question for discovery, never proof of a product failure. "},{"title":"Overview · The study, page by page","url":"/radio-mirchi#map","text":" Understand Business & leadership The company map, leadership, operating model, competitive assets and decisions a senior product leader needs to understand. Understand Revenue model A commercial breakdown of broadcast, integrated solutions, digital services, events, subscriptions and international monetisation. Understand Financials & economics Latest available Q2 / H1 FY27 results, FY26 context and the distinctions that make the numbers safe to discuss. Businesses Radio & advertiser value Broadcast economics, dayparts, audience measurement and a city-level advertiser growth approach. Businesses Events & IP portfolio Formats, portfolio examples, commercial mechanics, operating risks and a repeatable event growth model. Businesses Gaana, content & digital Gaana, Mirchi content, digital solutions and the difference between audience scale and subscription economics. Understand Users & customer needs Audience and buyer hypotheses to validate through research, support data, campaign history and actual behaviour. Understand Market & competition The market context and a practical comparison across radio, streaming, creators and live experiences. Evidence Web, mweb & app audit A platform-by-platform audit of public Mirchi and Gaana surfaces, with observed behaviour, business implications and explicit native-testing limits. Evidence Current initiatives A dedicated register of disclosed product updates, partnerships and campaigns, with the next question to ask rather than claiming each as a new idea. Recommend Prioritised opportunities Five growth bets, ranked provisionally with evidence, experiment design, dependencies and explicit stop conditions. Recommend First 90 days What I would do first, who needs to be involved and what would justify the next investment. Recommend KPIs & experiments Metric definitions, causal measurement and guardrails that connect product work to commercial outcomes. Prepare Economics lab Three interactive, illustrative models for an event edition, a paid subscriber cohort and radio inventory. No input is a forecast or an ENIL internal metric. Prepare Interview rehearsal A focused opening, role-specific discussion paths, fifteen practice answers and questions worth asking the panel. Prepare Why me How I would connect my experience to Mirchi’s needs, without overstating the evidence or assuming the role’s mandate. Evidence Sources & methodology Primary disclosures, live observations, app-store evidence and an explicit record of coverage limits. "},{"title":"Business & leadership · Get the entity and the brand right","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#company","text":" Layer What it means Interview implication Times Group / BCCL Promoter group context. ENIL is a separately listed company. S6 Do not treat every Times asset, dataset or client budget as automatically shared. ENIL Entertainment Network (India) Limited; BSE 532700, NSE ENIL. S2 Use ENIL when discussing disclosed company financials. Mirchi Radio, local personalities, brand solutions, content and live experiences. S7 The consumer brand is broader than a single FM frequency. Gaana Premium music and audio platform in ENIL’s portfolio. S5 Product economics include recurring payments, content costs and retention. Mirchi Plus / Mirchi Live Public content/app and event/campaign identities. S20 S12 Map the destination and user intent before proposing another app. The business has two important customers: people who give it attention and advertisers who pay to reach or engage them. Gaana also monetises the listener directly. This makes audience quality, commercial delivery and consumer trust interdependent. "},{"title":"Business & leadership · Know the leadership’s decision lens","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#leaders","text":" Leader Role in latest presentation Prepare to discuss Yatish Mehrishi Chief Executive Officer Portfolio choices, profitable growth, capital discipline. Preeti Nihalani Chief Operating Officer City execution, pricing, sales enablement and cross-functional delivery. Sumit Aggrawal Chief Strategy & Growth Officer Growth opportunities, partnerships and scalable operating models. Udit Tyagi Chief Digital Officer Digital product, technology and experimentation. Sanjay Ballabh Chief Financial Officer Margins, collections, cohort economics and investment trade-offs. Titles above follow the Q2 FY27 presentation; discussion themes are my preparation lenses, not stated individual mandates. S1 S8 "},{"title":"Business & leadership · What is difficult to reproduce","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#assets","text":" Analysis Local relevance A useful city personality understands language, humour, neighbourhoods and cultural timing. Treat that relationship as a product asset, with editorial judgment and talent continuity. Analysis Advertiser relationships A local sales relationship can open doors for several formats. The product challenge is making offers easy to understand, deliver and measure without fragmenting ownership. Analysis IP and execution A recognisable format can travel across cities, but execution depends on local demand, venue economics and sponsor fit. A repeatable playbook should preserve local relevance. "},{"title":"Business & leadership · A practical operating model to investigate","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#operations","text":" Central: product platform, analytics definitions, rights standards, billing rules, experimentation and reusable creative tooling. City: programming, local creators, advertiser relationships, event partners and cultural adaptation. Shared governance: deal approval, sponsorship fulfilment, audience permissions and contribution reporting. Decision rights: ask who owns the customer, product P&L, pricing, delivery SLA and cross-business revenue attribution. This is a proposed working model for discovery. It does not claim to describe ENIL’s current reporting lines. "},{"title":"Business & leadership · International: a local diaspora business","url":"/radio-mirchi/business#international","text":" ENIL’s public profile describes a presence in the USA, UAE, Qatar and Bahrain. Its FY26 operating review discusses diaspora engagement and partnership / licensing opportunities. These are company disclosures, not a fresh station-by-station international audit. S7 S5 Commercial lever Question to investigate Diaspora relevance Which language, music and community formats create a repeat habit in each market? Local advertiser demand What customer categories pay for access, and how concentrated are the accounts? Operating structure Which markets are owned, operated with partners, franchised or licensed, and who bears the cost? Rights and distribution Which content can cross borders, and on which digital or broadcast platforms? Capital discipline What local contribution, cash commitment and partner performance justify expansion? International growth should be evaluated market by market. A recognisable Indian brand can help acquisition, but local demand, rights and execution still determine the economics. "},{"title":"Revenue model · How the money is made","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#streams","text":" Engine Buyer / value purchased Revenue logic Costs and constraints Radio FCT Advertiser buys scheduled exposure to a city audience. Sold commercial seconds × realised net yield. Finite inventory, discounts, agency terms, seasonality, programming and station costs. Integrated brand solutions Brand buys an idea executed across RJ content, on-ground and digital touchpoints. Project fee, sponsorship package or contracted deliverables. Production, talent, vendors, revisions and delivery complexity. Events & IP Sponsors, ticket buyers and commercial partners. Sponsorship + net ticket receipts + contracted ancillary income. Artists, venue, production, permits, security, marketing, refunds and cash advances. Digital solutions Advertiser buys content, creators, inventory or managed campaign work. Campaign/service fee; recognise revenue according to contract and accounting policy. Creator fees, paid media, production, platform dependence; pass-through billing can inflate gross revenue. Gaana Listener or distribution partner buys premium access. Subscription / partnership consideration over service period. Rights, payment/channel fees, support, tech, acquisition and retention. International Local advertisers, partners and diaspora audiences. Market-specific operations, partnerships or licensing structures. Local regulation, rights, currency and partner economics. Business categories are grounded in ENIL disclosures; the formulas describe commercial mechanics and are analytical, not published ENIL rate cards. S7 S5 "},{"title":"Revenue model · The radio equation","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#radio-math","text":" Model Net FCT revenue = commercial seconds available × sell-through × realised revenue per second. Use the same city, daypart and time period for every input. A 5% price reduction needs more than 5% additional sold volume to keep revenue unchanged: 1 ÷ 0.95 − 1 = 5.26%. If capacity or listener ad tolerance is already constrained, the extra volume may not be achievable. Discounting should be evaluated against total contribution, advertiser retention and future pricing expectations. Sell-through and price are not independent. Prime time, local festivals, premium sponsorships and bundled contracts alter the inventory mix. A national average can hide both healthy cities and weak stations. "},{"title":"Revenue model · From advertiser brief to repeat budget","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#sales","text":" Step Product / process opportunity Commercial measure Define objective One city, one audience, one business outcome, one budget range. Qualified brief to proposal rate. Package offer Standard modules with explicit deliverables and optional custom work. Proposal time and gross contribution at quote. Approve & collect Margin review, advance collection and cancellation terms. Cash collected before committed vendor spend. Execute One delivery plan linking radio logs, creator assets and event tasks. On-time fulfilment and rework cost. Report & renew Show delivered media separately from response and causal lift. Repeat booking and renewal contribution. Recommended product principle: make the next purchase easier without promising attribution precision that the campaign design cannot support. "},{"title":"Revenue model · Questions that prevent misleading revenue stories","url":"/radio-mirchi/revenue#accounting","text":" Is ticket revenue shown gross or net of platform fees, taxes and organiser share? Is an event owned, co-produced, commissioned or only promoted? Branding alone does not establish IP ownership. Do digital solutions include media purchased on behalf of clients? Separate billings from retained margin. When is sponsorship cash collected versus recognised as revenue? Does a bundle pay Gaana on shipment, activation or usage? What is the effective net consideration? Are cross-sold revenues incremental or shifted from another Mirchi budget? "},{"title":"Financials & economics · Latest quarter: Q2 FY27","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#quarter","text":" Period: 1 July–30 September 2026. Released 3 November 2026. ₹ crore; ₹10 million = ₹1 crore. Figures below are presentation-defined operating income/revenue and EBITDA. S1 Metric Q2 FY27 Q2 FY26 YoY Consolidated operating revenue 116.70 141.14 −17.3% Consolidated EBITDA 12.05 11.38 +5.9% Consolidated PAT −4.86 −4.08 Loss widened Domestic operating revenue 113.65 135.42 −16.1% Domestic EBITDA 11.26 10.28 +9.5% Do not mix the headlines ₹11.3 crore / +9.5% is the rounded domestic EBITDA headline. ₹12.05 crore / +5.9% is consolidated EBITDA in the deck. Pair each profit number with the matching revenue scope. S1 S2 "},{"title":"Financials & economics · Full-year and half-year context","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#year","text":" Scope / period Operating revenue EBITDA PAT Consolidated FY26 565.17 44.96 −7.39 Consolidated FY25 544.15 78.56 11.95 Consolidated H1 FY27 230.39 21.08 −10.86 Consolidated H1 FY26 258.08 18.95 −9.36 FY26 from the Q4 deck; H1 from the Q2 deck. FY26 EBITDA declined despite revenue growth; H1 FY27 EBITDA improved while revenue declined. Annual results and a six-month period are not directly comparable. S4 S1 Calculated consolidated EBITDA margin: Q2 FY27 10.33% versus 8.06% a year earlier; FY26 7.96% versus FY25 14.44% . These are ratios of the displayed operating figures. EBITDA is not cash flow or PAT. "},{"title":"Financials & economics · What the portfolio mix says","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#mix","text":" Management reported approximately 53% radio and 29% digital in domestic Q2 revenue; the remaining approximately 18% covers events and other business. Digital revenue was about ₹33 crore and digital EBITDA loss about ₹7.5 crore. This is a rounded management mix, not a statutory segment reconciliation. S2 Radio 53% Digital 29% Other 18% Digital’s share can increase when radio declines. A higher percentage alone does not establish strong absolute digital growth. Evaluate growth, loss reduction and the quality of the acquired cohorts together. "},{"title":"Financials & economics · Cash, costs and the interview interpretation","url":"/radio-mirchi/financials#cash","text":" September consolidated cash was reported at ₹371.5 crore. For March, the Q4 deck distinguishes consolidated cash of about ₹423.9 crore from standalone cash of ₹404.2 crore. Avoid presenting them as two estimates of the same scope. S2 S4 Operating leverage: station and platform costs do not fall instantly with ad demand. Efficiency can improve EBITDA before revenue recovers. Below EBITDA: depreciation/amortisation, finance costs, other income, exceptional items and tax can move PAT differently. Event working capital: vendor advances create cash exposure before ticket and sponsor collections. Do not infer runway: cash balances are not an unrestricted product budget; commitments, lease liabilities and investment plans matter. The answer to practise “I see improving operating discipline, but I would not declare the transformation complete. I would track contribution and cash by business and cohort, while protecting the radio engine and proving repeatable economics in digital and events.” "},{"title":"Radio & advertiser value · What radio does well","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#role","text":" A useful radio proposition combines music with familiar personalities, local context, timely information and participation. The commercial product is access to that relationship. A listener who enjoys an RJ is not automatically a digital user or a ticket buyer; every handoff still has to earn the next action. The corporate profile lists 73 stations in 63 cities, with the listener figure on that page explicitly dated to IRS 2019. Use it to understand historical scale, not current unique reach. S7 "},{"title":"Radio & advertiser value · A senior PM’s radio dashboard","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#inventory","text":" Question Metric to inspect Decision Where is value leaking? City × station × daypart net yield, sell-through and contribution. Price, bundle or inventory allocation. Which advertisers repeat? Cohort repeat spend, category, account size and collections. Strengthen the proposition for valuable segments. Are campaigns delivered? Booked versus aired spots, make-goods and exceptions. Fix delivery reliability before expanding promises. What does the audience tolerate? Ad minutes, tune-out signals where measurable, complaints and listener research. Protect experience while selling inventory. Does a cross-channel campaign work? Tagged response and an agreed incrementality design. Prove impact at the appropriate confidence level. These are metrics to request internally. No internal dashboard or listening panel was available for this study. "},{"title":"Radio & advertiser value · Proposed pilot: a local advertiser return loop","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#pilot","text":" Analysis Customer need A local business needs a credible way to bring relevant people to a store or offer, and an easy way to decide whether to buy another campaign. It may have neither a marketing analyst nor a full agency. Analysis Minimum product Create a scoped campaign brief, a verified landing page or call response mechanism, a delivery log and a concise close-out report. Sell a bounded test before automating the entire sales process. Analysis Validation Select a small, comparable advertiser cohort; predefine one primary outcome. Use matched stores or time/geographic holdouts when practical. Report uncertainty, not just attributed clicks. Success criterion to agree before launch: higher incremental contribution from repeat advertisers with acceptable collection days, no rise in delivery exceptions and no deterioration in listener experience. "},{"title":"Radio & advertiser value · Rights and regulatory dependencies","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#constraints","text":" FM broadcast, online streaming, podcasts, social clips and event music can have different rights and contract conditions. Obtain a rights review for each intended reuse rather than treating a broadcast licence as permission for every platform. The government’s 2024 expansion announcement sets a 4% annual licence fee for the specified new-city channels. This must not be assumed to replace all existing ENIL licence obligations. S28 In an interview, ask how renewal exposure and regulatory changes enter capital allocation. Treat potential reforms as scenarios, not approved future savings. "},{"title":"Radio & advertiser value · Know the frequency, but check the city","url":"/radio-mirchi/radio#frequencies","text":" The September MIB list includes Mirchi at 98.3 MHz in Delhi, and at both 98.3 and 95 MHz in Bengaluru. Frequencies and brand variants vary by market; “98.3” is not the complete network map. S35 Before discussing a particular city, verify the current station, format, listener proposition and advertiser set. A second frequency should be evaluated on audience and commercial differentiation rather than assumed to be duplicate reach. "},{"title":"Events & IP portfolio · Know the portfolio and its status","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#portfolio","text":" Property / format Evidence / status Business lesson Mirchi Rock & Dhol 2026 Navratri listings across cities; now historical. S11 Cultural demand can support repeated city editions; pricing and costs remain local. Mirchi Neon Run District lists Chennai, 28 Nov 2026, 6 PM, from ₹299. Upcoming listing at research date. S26 Running plus entertainment can serve consumers and sponsors; verify the listing before attending. Mirchi Freshers S13 Campaign website and terms: 100 colleges, 16 cities, Aug–Sep 2026 period. S12 S13 A campus programme can join physical participation with a digital voting loop. Mirchi Music Awards Established IP; linked 16th-edition results are dated Dec 2024. S15 Recognisable content can generate sponsor and distribution value; no unverified 2026 edition claimed. SBI Green Marathon / Mindspace Eco Run Reported in Q4 FY26 presentation. S4 Commissioned or partner-led programmes can be commercially distinct from owned ticketed concerts. Mirchi Holicious BookMyShow 2026 listing marked event closed. S27 Ticket distribution is a separate relationship from the event brand. Spell Bee, concerts, corporate / RWA activations Established catalogue in company profile. S7 Several smaller formats can serve predictable advertiser needs without marquee concert risk. Royal Stag Boombox / Mirchi Club Nights Reported event / activation cases in Q4 FY26. S4 Different partner formats need different commercial contracts and delivery measures; association does not prove IP ownership. A portfolio mention does not prove ENIL owns every IP, all ticket proceeds or all execution economics. Contract structure must be checked event by event. "},{"title":"Events & IP portfolio · The event P&L that matters","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#economics","text":" Revenue / cost line What to verify Sponsorship Signed consideration, barter versus cash, deliverables, collections, cancellation clauses. Ticketing Paid admissions, average net yield, discounts, complimentary entries, refunds, platform fees and taxes. Ancillary Only contracted organiser share of stalls, hospitality or merchandise. Direct cost Artist, venue, stage, sound, production, permissions, security, medical, insurance and staffing. Marketing & selling Paid media, commissions, creative and attributable sales cost. Downside Weather, cancellation, artist non-appearance, demand shortfall and vendor commitments. Cash & overhead Timing of advances and settlements; show contribution separately from allocated corporate overhead. The live calculator uses a simplified pre-tax contribution model. It is an illustration, not Mirchi’s actual event cost structure. Open event economics lab . "},{"title":"Events & IP portfolio · The attendee journey is the retention product","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#journey","text":" Discover: relevant city, format, date, artist and accessible information; explain why this event fits the person. Decide: show total price, inclusions, age/access rules, transport information and cancellation terms before checkout. Attend: ticket retrieval, entry throughput, clear help, safe capacity, water and medical support. Remember: useful post-event content and feedback; obtain permission for future contact. Return: recommend the next relevant event, not every event nationwide. Reward repeat attendance only when incremental margin pays for the benefit. "},{"title":"Events & IP portfolio · Proposed event growth system","url":"/radio-mirchi/events#scale","text":" Start with one repeatable format in two contrasting cities. Give every edition a signed sponsor plan, a downside P&L, a cash exposure ceiling and an attendee service plan. Link the promotion source to a first-party or partner-compliant event record so the team can understand conversion without double-counting. Analysis Before go / no-go Secure minimum sponsorship and venue options. Track break-even paid admissions against realistic demand, then set spend-release gates. Analysis During execution Use one operating checklist with named owners. Escalate queues, safety, artist delays and fulfilment gaps quickly. Capture only the data necessary for the intended service. Analysis After the edition Close collections, vendor settlements and sponsor fulfilment. Compare realised contribution with the quote and track sponsor / attendee return over subsequent editions. "},{"title":"Gaana, content & digital · Three digital jobs, three business models","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#portfolio","text":" Subscription Gaana A consumer pays for a useful audio experience. Discovery, playback reliability, entitlement and repeat listening determine value and renewal. The annual report describes a subscription-led service. S5 Audience & content Mirchi content Articles, personalities, stories and social clips attract attention and can lead into deeper listening. The Mirchi web root currently leads to Reads with Gaana navigation. S21 B2B services Digital solutions A brand pays for a campaign or service. The product is reliable creative and commercial delivery, not necessarily another consumer application. S2 "},{"title":"Gaana, content & digital · What the public price surfaces showed","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#pricing","text":" Surface Observed price / proposition Interpretation Gaana web trial ₹1 / 30-day trial; says yearly auto-renew after trial. Verify the next charge and mandate terms at checkout; no checkout completed. Gaana web yearly ₹709 offer; ₹799 reference price. An observed offer, not realised ARPU. Gaana web monthly ₹129; monthly auto-renew. A different duration and commitment. Gaana web one-time annual ₹899; no auto debit. Existing customer choice; do not propose this as absent. Noise × Gaana ₹1,399 hardware bundle with one year Gaana Plus. Separate hardware price from consideration earned by Gaana. Gaana iOS listing SKUs include ₹119 monthly / ₹799 yearly. Listing SKUs can differ from web and selected checkout eligibility. Web prices from this session, bundle from the Oct announcement, iOS SKUs from the India listing. Taxes, eligibility and offer duration must be checked in the selected purchase journey. S23 S10 S19 "},{"title":"Gaana, content & digital · Proposed activation and retention sequence","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#growth","text":" Stage Customer value Measurement Intent Preserve the artist, song, podcast or language that brought the user. Source-linked intent to a successful content start. Activation Get to a satisfying listening session quickly. Time to first successful play; entitlement success. Habit Make returning easy through existing history, queue and discovery capabilities. Retained listening days and successful sessions per cohort. Paid value Explain what the selected plan gives and when it renews. Contribution per paid user, disputes and refund requests. Renewal Reconnect the person with value they used; easy account control. Paid renewal contribution after costs and incentives. History and queue improvements already appear in company updates. The opportunity is to validate which users benefit and whether those benefits change retention. S4 "},{"title":"Gaana, content & digital · Content IP can bridge attention and payment","url":"/radio-mirchi/digital#content","text":" Sunday Suspense continues to publish: the 17 November Indrapatan announcement points audiences to Mirchi Bangla YouTube and Gaana. This is evidence of an active regional franchise, not an estimate of its commercial performance. S14 Proposed test: preserve a listener’s chosen story or creator through a web-to-app handoff, resume them at the relevant destination and measure qualified listening and subsequent renewal. Keep a clean holdout to distinguish genuine incremental activity from users who would have listened anyway. Do not equate these metrics Social followers, YouTube subscribers, monthly active listeners, trials, paid subscribers and billed subscribers measure different populations. Never use one as a substitute for another, and do not add platform counts into unique reach. "},{"title":"Users & customer needs · The customer map","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#needs","text":" Customer Job to be done What good looks like Research to run Local listener / commuter “Keep me company and connected to my city.” Relevant hosts, easy tuning, predictable experience. Diary study by commute / daypart, city and language. Music subscriber “Play something I want, quickly, without interruptions.” Relevant discovery, reliable playback and clear access. Task tests plus funnel and entitlement cohorts. Story / RJ fan “Let me follow this voice or series wherever I am.” Correct episode, continuity and meaningful release alerts. Follow one series from social discovery to repeat listening. Event attendee “Help me choose a worthwhile, smooth outing.” Clear price and rules, dependable entry and experience. Journey interviews including non-buyers and no-shows. Advertiser / agency “Reach the right people and justify the next budget.” Clear scope, dependable delivery and honest measurement. Win/loss interviews and repeat-spend analysis. Sponsor “Own an audience moment with credible value.” Contracted visibility, engagement and documented fulfilment. Sponsor review before and after each edition. RJ / creator / operations team “Help me make and deliver quality work efficiently.” Fast tools, rights clarity, fair control and fewer handoffs. Observe real production and campaign workflows. These are needs-based hypotheses, not claims from completed customer interviews. "},{"title":"Users & customer needs · Segment by behaviour before adding demographics","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#segmentation","text":" Audio: language, entry intent, content affinity, time of day, device, connection quality and paid status. Events: city, group size, format, first versus repeat attendance, purchase lead time and budget. Advertisers: objective, category, geography, budget, buying frequency, agency involvement and credit profile. Partnership cohorts: redemption, listening activation, service duration, renewal eligibility and contribution. A single retention number can hide a strong existing subscriber base and a weak partner-acquired cohort. Define the population and the moment the clock starts before comparing groups. "},{"title":"Users & customer needs · Discovery plan with evidence standards","url":"/radio-mirchi/users#research","text":" Analysis Qualitative Interview customers who completed the job and those who abandoned it. Observe the task rather than asking which feature they want. Recruit beyond vocal fans and recent complainants. Analysis Quantitative Validate event and account identity, payment outcomes and instrumentation before using funnels. Segment by channel and release version so a rollout does not look like a behavioural trend. Analysis Decision Write the evidence that would change the proposed priority. A hypothesis should be easy to reject when research shows the need is small, already met or too costly to serve. "},{"title":"Market & competition · The market is moving at different speeds","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#market","text":" FICCI–EY estimates India’s 2025 M&E market at ₹2.78 trillion. Its March 2026 release reports radio down 7% to ₹23 billion, live events up 44%, and digital advertising up 26%. These are calendar-year industry estimates; they are not Mirchi growth rates. S9 Inference: diversification is commercially sensible, but an attractive category does not make every entrant or format profitable. Mirchi should choose businesses where its relationships, IP and city execution create an advantage after incremental cost. "},{"title":"Market & competition · Competition by customer decision","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#landscape","text":" Arena Relevant alternatives What they compete on Mirchi question Local advertising Radio City, RED FM, BIG FM, Fever, regional stations, local publishers, outdoor and digital ads. S29 S30 Local reach, price, targeting, creative, delivery and evidence. Why should a local advertiser renew this package? Audio habit Spotify, YouTube / YouTube Music, JioSaavn, Apple Music, Amazon Music and other audio services. Catalogue, discovery, devices, reliability, price and convenience. Which listening job can Gaana serve especially well? Creator attention YouTube, Instagram and independent regional creators. Creator affinity, entertainment, distribution and community. Can the creator relationship lead to an owned, useful service? Going out Concert promoters, local organisers, BookMyShow and District discovery. S26 S27 Relevant supply, trust, availability, convenience and price. Where does Mirchi add distinctive IP or execution value? Brand solutions Agencies, creator networks and platforms. Strategy, creative quality, speed, measurement and commercial terms. Can integrated local delivery justify a better margin? Station-level examples are corroborated by the MIB list; verify the specific city because licences and operating footprints can change. S35 This is a substitute map, not a market-share ranking. No current competitor price, audience size or financial claim is inferred without a source. "},{"title":"Market & competition · A defensible position to test","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#position","text":" Analysis Win locally Connect an advertiser’s city objective with a credible host, useful local content and a relevant experience. Make delivery and response visible. Analysis Win through culture Use regional voices and recognisable franchises to create a reason to return. Avoid a feature race with every large audio platform. Analysis Win through execution A consistent operational experience can make a format easier for sponsors and attendees to repeat. Build repeatability around margin and service quality. "},{"title":"Market & competition · SWOT, tied to decisions","url":"/radio-mirchi/competition#swot","text":" Lens Assessment Decision implication Strengths Brand, cultural relevance, local talent, advertiser relationships, content and execution capabilities. Build around existing advantages rather than unrelated software products. Weaknesses to investigate Cross-platform continuity, variable economics by business, execution complexity. Measure before calling them proven failures. Opportunities Better conversion of existing reach, retained paid cohorts, repeat sponsor formats. Pilot focused improvements with contribution as the success measure. Threats Ad-budget shifts, creator/platform dependence, rights costs, event competition and demand volatility. Use scenario planning, diversified channels and explicit downside limits. "},{"title":"Web, mweb & app audit · Platform coverage and depth","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#coverage","text":" Surface What was checked Depth / outcome Mirchi desktop web Root, Reads, navigation, subscription handoff, mobile-app landing. Live browser at default 1280 × 720. Root leads to /stories; Gaana links and app QR visible. S21 S20 Mirchi mobile web Reads and app handoff at 390 × 844. Responsive browser emulation; document width 390px. No physical handset used. S21 Gaana desktop web Home, plan page, radio, podcast listing, series detail and app-store links. Live public journey. Subscription options and sign-in controls inspected; no payment. S22 S23 S24 S25 Gaana mobile web Public discovery and navigation at 390 × 844. Responsive controls observed. Radio document measured 728px wide at 390px viewport; reproduce and isolate overflow before grading severity. S24 Mirchi Android Listing, metadata, update date, rating and description. Live listing inspected. Installed app, OTP, playback and offline mode not tested. S16 Mirchi iOS Website handoff and India / Qatar storefront availability. India URL showed page not found; Qatar listing accessible. No universal delisting conclusion. S17 S20 Gaana Android Listing, current release notes and declared features. Public store evidence. No installed Android / Android Auto test. S18 Gaana iOS / iPad / Watch India listing, version history, supported devices and purchase SKUs. Listing evidence; no native iPhone, iPad, Watch or CarPlay execution. S19 Gaana TV / OEM distribution Samsung TV and Vivo disclosures. Company-reported availability; device-level experience not exercised. S1 Mirchi Live / Freshers Home, campus page, participation form fields and voting information. Live browser. No selfie uploaded, consent accepted, registration or vote submitted. S12 S13 Ticket distribution District Neon Run listing and Book tickets flow; BookMyShow historical event. District ticket types observed before purchase; location prompt encountered. No tickets added or paid. S26 S27 Social / creator distribution Mirchi Bangla YouTube; Mirchi Plus and Gaana Instagram; official Gaana footer links. Public profile / content inspected. Not a census of every city, RJ and language account. S31 S33 S22 Corporate / investor web Company profile, leadership, filings, annual and investor materials. Primary-source document review. S7 S8 S1 S4 S5 "},{"title":"Web, mweb & app audit · Observed findings, without overstating impact","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#observations","text":" Observed / needs validation O1 · Mirchi-to-Gaana transition Mirchi Reads uses Gaana navigation and subscription calls to action; the separate app landing still promotes Mirchi Plus. That is an observed mixed destination story, not proof users are confused. S21 S20 Validate: can a new user explain which app they need and preserve their intended content through the handoff? Measure: destination success and retained listening. Observed / scoped O2 · Mobile accessibility constraint Mirchi Reads declares a viewport with user-scalable=no. At 390px, the first article heading appeared around 522px from the top in this session, following navigation and an ad region. S21 Validate: pinch / browser zoom and first-content visibility on real devices with and without ads. Test: allow zoom and reduce non-content space while monitoring ad contribution. Observed / region-specific O3 · App availability needs a regional check The India Mirchi iOS URL returned page not found; the app-download landing links a US storefront, while Qatar metadata remains accessible. S17 S20 Validate: the intended India migration / app policy, current installation paths and deep-link fallbacks. A regional unavailable page is not evidence that all apps are discontinued. Observed / checkout untested O4 · Existing plan choice is substantial Gaana web showed trial, recurring and one-time annual choices. Cancellation guidance was present in its public FAQ. S23 Validate: selected renewal amount, mandate comprehension, purchase restore and actual cancellation tasks. Presence of a choice does not prove the complete task works. Observed / partial playback O5 · A regional story plays publicly Sunday Suspense Bangla series and episodes were visible. A brief play test advanced the HTML audio clock with readyState 4. S25 Limit: this demonstrates a browser playback start in this session, not full-length access, audible quality, native playback or offline entitlement. Content-level access may vary. Observed / status question O6 · Campaign status needs reconciliation Freshers home displayed a live campus and completed campuses, while published terms gave a tentative September end. S12 S13 Validate: whether terms were extended and ensure the displayed status, eligibility and current legal period agree. Do not label the campaign inactive solely from the tentative date. "},{"title":"Web, mweb & app audit · App evidence: current release versus legacy storefront","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#apps","text":" App / surface Snapshot What it does and does not establish Mirchi Plus Android Live browser: 2.9 stars, ~1.82K reviews, 1M+ downloads; update 30 Mar 2024. S16 A legacy public listing remains. Search cache differed; rating is not a full user-sentiment study. Mirchi Plus iOS Qatar Version 7.5, 1 Apr 2024. S17 Regional metadata only. India availability could not be established. Gaana Android 4.2 stars, 100M+ downloads; retrieved update 4 Nov 2026. S18 Active release metadata and large lifetime distribution. Downloads do not equal active or paying listeners. Gaana iOS India 4.1 stars, ~114K ratings; version 9.26.4 shown two days ago. S19 Current release evidence, supported devices and store SKUs. Not installed-app QA. Reviews: avoid a false finding The public pages surfaced old featured reviews as well as current metadata. I did not scrape a recent, deduplicated representative sample, so I do not claim that historical billing, ads or playback complaints describe the current release. "},{"title":"Web, mweb & app audit · Cross-platform test cases to complete with devices and accounts","url":"/radio-mirchi/platforms#journeys","text":" Journey Required checks Business reason Acquire / restore Web, Android, iOS; phone / email identity; existing subscriber restore; partner redemption; source intent. Prevent paid or partner users from losing access. Listen First play, queue, search, language, resume, background, Bluetooth, lock screen, interruption and weak network. Prove the listening habit works in the actual context. Offline / devices Download, airplane mode, expiry, device switch; Watch / TV / car where supported. Verify the paid promise and device-specific continuity. Billing control Full renewal disclosure, mandate, receipt, cancellation, restore and support escalation. Protect trust and reliable recurring revenue. Attend / return Social / radio source, event detail, booking platform, total price, ticket retrieval, entry and post-event communication. Connect conversion to a useful experience and a return relationship. Participate Current eligibility, optional permissions, photo flow, voting rules, error states and consent records. Make campaign participation clear and operationally trustworthy. These cases remain a native / authenticated validation plan. The public audit does not claim they passed. "},{"title":"Current initiatives · Current and recent initiative register","url":"/radio-mirchi/initiatives#register","text":" Filter initiatives All initiatives Gaana product & distribution Mirchi & local campaigns Events & participation Launched, Oct 2026 Noise bundle One-year premium bundle. S10 Question to build on it How many eligible purchasers redeem, activate, retain and later renew? Reported Q2 FY27 Samsung TV + Vivo distribution TV availability; phone pre-installation. S1 Question to build on it Do device cohorts produce incremental, profitable listening after acquisition cost? Reported Q2 FY27 Queue & mood controls Contextual queue updates. S1 Question to build on it Which contexts improve successful listening and paid retention? Reported Q2 FY27 UMG early access Selected releases 72 hours early. S1 Question to build on it Does exclusivity change paid conversion or just shift listening time? Reported Q2 FY27 DISCVR / Off The Record / Unplugged Artist-led formats. S1 Question to build on it Which formats create retained listeners after production cost? Reported Q4 FY26 Web 2.0 / listening history / lyrics search Web, resumption and discovery upgrades. S4 Question to build on it Have time to successful play and repeat sessions improved? Reported Q2 FY27 Mirchi Par AI-GIRI Delhi AI content campaign. S1 Question to build on it Can engagement become a useful recurring local content franchise? Reported Q2 FY27 Vriksha Bandhan Mumbai tree-adoption campaign. S1 Question to build on it What sponsor and participant outcomes survive after campaign completion? Reported Q2 FY27 Border Podcast Chandigarh listener experience. S1 Question to build on it Which parts are repeatable without losing authenticity or safety? Reported Q2 FY27 Vocal for Local / Telugu Language Day Local business and cultural campaigns. S1 Question to build on it Does the local relationship translate into repeat advertiser or audience value? 2026 campaign; terms Aug–Sep Mirchi Freshers Season 13 Campus participation and voting. S12 Question to build on it What portion of participation converts into sponsor value and permitted repeat engagement? Past October listings Rock & Dhol 2026 Multi-city festive format. S11 Question to build on it Which cities and editions met contribution and attendee-service targets? Reported Q4 FY26 SBI Green Marathon / Mindspace Eco Run Partner event programmes. S4 Question to build on it How do contractual delivery, repeat sponsorship and cash exposure compare? Upcoming listing: 28 Nov Mirchi Neon Run Chennai Ticketed neon running experience. S26 Question to build on it What is the break-even paid attendance and signed sponsor coverage? Published 17 Nov 2026 Sunday Suspense: Indrapatan YouTube and Gaana release. S14 Question to build on it Can a story-specific handoff increase retained listening? "},{"title":"Current initiatives · How to discuss existing work in the interview","url":"/radio-mirchi/initiatives#respect","text":" Useful framing “I saw the work already underway. My proposal builds on that investment: define the intended customer behaviour, instrument the handoff, compare cohorts and scale the profitable result.” Do not pitch AI, a non-renewing annual plan, better recommendations, a regional story franchise or a hardware partnership as if Mirchi has never considered them. Establish what is live, what is announced and what outcome is still being validated. "},{"title":"Prioritised opportunities · Provisional priority order","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#priorities","text":" Priority Customer problem / opportunity Why this order Evidence status P1 · Gaana activation A partner-acquired user needs to redeem and reach the content they want. Existing distribution investment; measurable end-to-end outcome. Partnership exists; friction magnitude not yet measured. S10 P1 · Advertiser repeat spend Advertiser needs a dependable campaign and clear reason to buy again. Commercial usefulness can benefit the current engine. Need hypothesis; validate against account cohorts. P2 · Event repeatability Sponsor and attendee need predictable execution and value. Build on existing formats before adding capital-heavy new IP. Events exist; edition-level economics unknown publicly. S11 S26 P2 · Content continuity Fan needs the exact story / creator after crossing platforms. Can connect regional content with repeat listening. Distribution observed; conversion effect unproven. S14 Enabler · Production tooling Creators and operators need fewer repetitive handoffs. Pilot only on measured cost or turnaround bottlenecks. Workflow hypothesis, not an assertion of current inefficiency. Ranks reflect potential decision value and existing capabilities. They are not a fabricated RICE score; actual reach, engineering effort and baseline economics would determine final prioritisation. "},{"title":"Prioritised opportunities · Bet 1: distribution to retained listening","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#activation","text":" Analysis Smallest useful release A partner redemption journey that preserves campaign and content intent, validates entitlement, and helps the listener reach a first successful session. Reuse the existing app and subscription stack. Analysis Test and owner Product, partnerships, growth, billing and analytics define eligible cohorts. Compare the new journey with the current journey, keeping pricing and partner eligibility stable. Analysis Scale / stop Scale when retained contribution per eligible purchaser improves after partner and incentive costs. Stop if redemption rises but paid retention, support cost or contribution deteriorates. Proposed metric hierarchy: eligible buyers → reachable redemption → activated account → successful play → retained listening → contribution after the service period → paid renewal. Do not call a complimentary year a paid conversion. "},{"title":"Prioritised opportunities · Bet 2: a measurable local advertiser package","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#advertiser","text":" Offer a limited catalogue by objective, city and budget, supported by a clear delivery plan and response measurement. Start with a category that repeats frequently enough to evaluate within a practical window. A sales-assisted workflow is a reasonable first version; self-service comes after the offer is repeatable. Primary: incremental 90-day advertiser contribution and repeat booking. Guardrails: collection days, deal discount, delivery exceptions, sales time and listener experience. Evidence: matched accounts or a phased rollout; track displaced radio or solution spend. Stop: higher gross billings with lower retained margin or longer credit exposure. "},{"title":"Prioritised opportunities · Bet 3: repeatable event editions","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#events","text":" Put event discovery, booking partners, sponsor fulfilment and the edition P&L into one operating view. Preserve attendee consent and ticket-platform contractual boundaries. The product should support a faster, better go/no-go decision, not merely make another listing page. Primary: realised edition contribution and cash conversion. Customer: entry wait, issue resolution, sponsor fulfilment and subsequent return. Scale: comparable editions meet economics and service gates across cities. Stop: the model depends on uncontracted sponsorship, unrealistic attendance or unsustainable local workload. "},{"title":"Prioritised opportunities · Bet 4 / 5: content continuity and useful AI","url":"/radio-mirchi/opportunities#ai","text":" For content continuity, start with one franchise and preserve the destination from social post to story page to app. For AI, observe a real workflow first: transcription, clip selection, tagging, local adaptation or campaign report assembly may be candidates. Compare turnaround and error rate against the current process. Quality and rights are part of the product Keep editorial review, talent permission, licensed-use boundaries and factual checks in the release criteria. A faster output is valuable only if it is usable and creates no extra correction or rights burden. "},{"title":"First 90 days · The plan","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#sequence","text":" Window Work Concrete output Gate Days 1–15 Agree mandate; meet commercial, content, events, digital, finance and city teams. Observe customer and internal journeys. Business tree, metric definitions, platform inventory, baseline data-quality review. One accountable owner and reliable success measure per pilot. Days 16–30 Size the top two needs; validate existing work; agree counterfactual and cash exposure. Pilot briefs, baseline cohorts, tracking design, cost / benefit ranges, stop rules. Approve one consumer and one commercial pilot only if capacity permits. Days 31–60 Ship bounded changes; instrument entitlement and delivery; monitor service quality. Working activation journey or advertiser workflow; weekly economics review. Results are measurable and guardrails stable before more traffic or cities. Days 61–90 Read mature-enough cohorts; close sponsor/vendor cash loops; compare rollout groups. Decision memo: scale, iterate or stop; owner, budget and next-quarter plan. Scale by incremental contribution and customer value, not activity counts. Annual Gaana renewal cannot be proved in 90 days. Use short-term activation and retention as leading indicators, maintain the cohort for later renewal measurement and avoid claiming validated lifetime value too early. "},{"title":"First 90 days · Operating cadence","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#cadence","text":" Analysis Weekly business review A compact dashboard: commercial contribution and collections; consumer activation and retention; delivery exceptions; experiment status; key dependencies. Discuss decisions and surprises, not a catalogue of activities. Analysis Fortnightly learning review Show one customer journey or workflow observation, test results and what changed in the hypothesis. Include negative evidence and experiments stopped. Analysis Monthly portfolio review Compare investment and returns by business. Protect committed delivery, revisit capital exposure and stop pilots that are not earning the next tranche of effort. "},{"title":"First 90 days · Collaboration and decision rights","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#stakeholders","text":" Partner What to agree Finance Revenue definitions, contribution waterfall, cash timing and investment hurdle. Sales & agencies Customer need, offer scope, pricing authority and renewal ownership. Content / RJs Editorial quality, local adaptation, workload and talent rights. Events & city teams Safety and service requirements, vendors, venue constraints and escalation owners. Engineering / design / data Smallest release, instrumentation quality and operational support. Partnerships / legal Entitlement terms, distribution measurement and permitted data use. Dependencies are part of prioritisation. A high-impact idea that requires unready billing, rights or partner data may need a smaller first step. "},{"title":"First 90 days · What I would resolve before promising a roadmap","url":"/radio-mirchi/plan#questions","text":" Which business and P&L does this role own? What outcome would make the hiring manager call the first quarter successful? Which teams and systems can the role directly influence? What product work is already committed or in flight? Which metrics are trusted, and where do teams disagree on definitions? Which city / audience / advertiser segment is most strategically important now? "},{"title":"KPIs & experiments · The KPI tree","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#tree","text":" Business Outcome Leading measures Guardrails Radio Contribution from retained advertisers Net yield, sell-through, repeat spend, delivery. Ad load, discount leakage, credit days, make-goods. Events Realised edition contribution and cash recovery Paid attendance, net ticket yield, sponsor collections, repeat intent. Safety, entry wait, refunds, vendor exposure, fulfilment. Gaana Retained subscriber contribution Intent-to-play, entitlement success, retained listening days, renewal cohorts. Playback reliability, support cost, refunds, partner economics. Digital solutions Retained gross contribution per client Proposal speed, win rate, repeat scope, on-time delivery. Pass-through spend, rework, collections and concentration. Content Useful retained audience and attributable commercial value Repeat consumption, series completion, qualified handoffs. Rights, quality, creator workload and platform dependence. A proposed shared lens is incremental contribution from repeat customer relationships . It needs a business-specific definition; a sponsor, an advertiser and a subscriber cannot share one denominator. "},{"title":"KPIs & experiments · Definitions that need to be explicit","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#definitions","text":" Activation: a successful value moment, not an install or a login. Define the required listening or campaign outcome before measurement. Retention: the fraction of a starting cohort that meets the defined value event in a later window. Keep trial, partner and paid cohorts separate. Contribution: net recognised revenue minus the costs included in the agreed waterfall. State which variable, direct and allocated costs are included. Incrementality: the change versus a credible counterfactual, not the number of people with a campaign tag. Repeat event customer: a deduplicated person attending a second relevant edition with permitted identity linkage. Net yield: realised revenue after discounts and the adjustments agreed with finance. "},{"title":"KPIs & experiments · Three experiments worth designing properly","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#experiments","text":" Experiment Primary test Design caution Partner activation journey Incremental retained contribution per eligible cohort. Randomise or phase within comparable partner cohorts; preserve offer and season. Advertiser package 90-day repeat contribution versus current offer. Account for sales selection, account size and budget cannibalisation. Event reminder / return loop Incremental net ticket contribution from permitted audience. Use a holdout; include discount cost, refunds and substitution between events. Choose sample size from the actual baseline, a meaningful minimum detectable effect, allocation and desired statistical precision. No sample-size number is invented here. Predefine the decision window and guardrails, and avoid repeatedly stopping the test at the first positive result. "},{"title":"KPIs & experiments · Honest attribution across offline and online","url":"/radio-mirchi/metrics#attribution","text":" On-air codes, tagged links, unique landing pages, booking references and CRM matching can identify observed response. They do not automatically capture all radio exposure or establish causation. Pair response tracking with holdouts or matched comparisons where feasible, and report uncertainty. The stakeholder-friendly dashboard Show what was delivered, what people did, what changed versus the comparison and how much contribution remained. Keep these four layers separate so a reach metric does not quietly become a revenue claim. "},{"title":"Economics lab · Event edition: contribution and break-even","url":"/radio-mirchi/lab#events","text":" All amounts are in rupees, excluding GST. Ticket price is net organiser receipt; no fees or taxes are deducted again. Variable cost is per paid attendee. Sponsorship and ancillary income must be contracted; allocated corporate overhead is excluded. Paid ticket capacity Paid occupancy (%) Net receipt per ticket (₹) Sponsorship (₹) Net ancillary income (₹) Fixed direct costs (₹) Variable cost per attendee (₹) Reset event assumptions Formula: contribution = paid attendees × (net ticket receipt − variable cost) + sponsorship + ancillary − fixed costs. Break-even attendees = ceiling(max(0, fixed − sponsorship − ancillary) ÷ ticket contribution), subject to positive ticket contribution and capacity. "},{"title":"Economics lab · Subscriber cohort: first-year contribution","url":"/radio-mirchi/lab#subscribers","text":" This model starts with paying users. It is not suitable for treating a complimentary hardware bundle as full-price revenue. Annual price below is net recognised service revenue per paid year, excluding taxes. Cost-share and retention inputs are hypothetical, not Gaana disclosures. Starting paid users Annual net service revenue (₹) One-year paid renewal (%) Variable revenue-linked costs (%) Annual service cost per user (₹) Acquisition cost per starting user (₹) Reset subscriber assumptions Formula: annual unit contribution before acquisition = annual net revenue × (1 − variable cost share) − annual service cost. First-year cohort contribution subtracts acquisition spend. Renewal illustration applies the same unit economics to renewing users, excludes new acquisition and is not lifetime value. "},{"title":"Economics lab · Radio: sell-through versus price","url":"/radio-mirchi/lab#inventory","text":" An illustrative period with a fixed pool of available commercial seconds. Changing utilisation and yield does not account for changes in station, daypart, inventory quality, collections or incremental operating costs. Available commercial seconds Sell-through (%) Net revenue per second (₹) Alternative sell-through (%) Alternative price discount (%) Reset radio assumptions Decision rule A revenue increase does not establish a profit increase. Use these models to expose assumptions, then add the actual cost, cash and customer constraints before recommending a decision. "},{"title":"Interview rehearsal · My 90-second opening","url":"/radio-mirchi/interview#opening","text":" “My background sits at the intersection of product, subscription growth and hands-on execution. I have worked on consumer journeys at Times Internet and D2C growth at VAHDAM, and I also build products myself. What interests me about Mirchi is the combination of local trust, creators, advertisers and live experiences. From the latest ENIL results, I see a business diversifying while working hard on profitability. I would approach radio, events, digital solutions and Gaana as different economic engines, then identify where shared relationships and content can create repeat customer value. I have looked at the work already underway, including Gaana product updates, distribution partnerships, regional content and live formats. My starting point would be to understand your mandate and data, then choose a focused customer or commercial journey, ship a bounded improvement and measure contribution as well as customer experience. I would like to bring both the analytical discipline and the ability to build and deliver that work.” Personal positioning is based on Anchit’s provided career context. Use only metrics you can substantiate from your own work; the site’s About page links the portfolio. "},{"title":"Interview rehearsal · Practice questions and answer frameworks","url":"/radio-mirchi/interview#answers","text":" Pick a practice question Expand all answers Practise aloud: conclusion, evidence, decision, measurement. How would you describe Mirchi’s business? I see ENIL as a city-centric entertainment and advertiser company with radio as a foundation, alongside events, digital solutions and Gaana. I would understand each P&L separately and use the shared assets—local relationships, creators and IP—to improve repeat customer value. What stood out in the latest financial results? Q2 FY27 consolidated operating revenue was ₹116.70 crore, down 17.3%, while consolidated EBITDA was ₹12.05 crore, up 5.9%. The domestic headline is different: ₹11.26 crore EBITDA, up 9.5%. I would read that as improving operating discipline in a weak revenue environment, while watching net losses and sustainable demand. S1 What would you improve first? I would confirm the mandate and baseline, then pick a bounded journey. Given existing Gaana distribution work, partner redemption to retained listening is a strong candidate. For a commercial remit, I would prioritise an advertiser repeat-spend or event economics workflow. I would not choose before seeing cohort contribution and current commitments. How would you grow event revenue? Start by separating owned IP, commissioned work and promoted partner events. For each city edition, understand sponsor commitments, net ticket yield, break-even attendance and cash advances. Grow the formats that earn repeat attendance and sponsor renewal at acceptable contribution and service quality. Would you build a new Mirchi super-app? I would first test whether the need can be served through existing Mirchi, Gaana and booking journeys. Another app introduces acquisition, entitlement and maintenance work. I would invest in a new surface only if a validated cross-business job needs it and existing surfaces cannot serve it economically. How would you evaluate the Noise partnership? Separate potential reach, devices sold, eligible buyers, redemptions, activated listeners and renewals. A complimentary year is not a paid conversion. Compare retained contribution by cohort after partner terms, content and support costs, and keep measuring beyond the first 90 days. What is your view on radio’s future? Radio can remain valuable where a city audience trusts its personalities and timely local context. I would improve the commercial proposition and delivery proof while protecting listener value. I would also recognise advertising pressure rather than assume the medium will recover automatically. Where would you use AI? I would observe content and campaign workflows, then test a specific bottleneck such as transcription, tagging or report preparation. I would measure usable turnaround time and correction burden, keep editorial and talent controls, and scale only if the quality-adjusted economics improve. How do you prioritise without internal data? Use public evidence to form hypotheses, not a confident backlog. Define the customer need, likely economic lever, dependency and cheapest validation. Replace provisional priority with measured reach, effort, baseline performance and contribution once inside the company. What would you not claim from this study? I have not measured native app playback, billing recovery, cancellations or Mirchi’s internal funnels. Store ratings are snapshots; old featured reviews are not a recent defect census. I would bring these as targeted research questions rather than claim they prove current user pain. How does your experience connect? My background connects subscription growth, consumer journeys and hands-on product delivery. ET work helps me reason about repeat paid value and conversion; D2C work helps with acquisition and lifecycle economics. I would bring that approach to Mirchi while learning its radio, event and rights-specific operating realities. Why Mirchi? Mirchi sits at an interesting intersection of people, local culture and commercial execution. The opportunity I find compelling is connecting that existing strength with better customer journeys and measurable economics. I would like to own a clear business outcome and build the smallest useful product that moves it. How do you handle sales versus product priorities? Agree the customer promise, delivery cost and success measure together. Distinguish a reusable product requirement from a one-client custom request. If custom work is commercially justified, price and staff it explicitly instead of hiding it inside the roadmap. What is the biggest risk in diversification? New revenue can carry lower margins, larger operational complexity or more cash exposure. I would look at incremental contribution and capital requirements, and avoid celebrating a larger non-radio percentage just because the radio denominator fell. What would make you stop a pilot? A failed customer need, no credible measurement, worse contribution, repeated service issues or an unready rights / billing dependency. I would document the learning and stop quickly enough to protect capacity and customer trust. "},{"title":"Interview rehearsal · Adapt to the role the panel describes","url":"/radio-mirchi/interview#role","text":" Remit Lead with Bring proof from your experience Product / digital Activation, playback and entitlement, retained cohorts, experimentation. A journey you diagnosed, built and measured. Growth / revenue Repeat advertiser contribution, paid acquisition, distribution economics. A commercial funnel with a defensible baseline and result. Events / IP Edition economics, sponsor value, attendee service and operational delivery. Your actual ownership, collaborators and constraints. Business leadership Portfolio trade-offs, capital discipline, operating model and execution cadence. A cross-functional decision you made under uncertainty. The exact interview role and panel were not supplied. The study covers these paths without assuming one job description. "},{"title":"Interview rehearsal · Questions to ask the interviewers","url":"/radio-mirchi/interview#ask","text":" Which outcome does this role own directly, and which business is the priority? Where do you see the biggest gap today: demand, product experience, monetisation or operating execution? How are Gaana partner cohorts evaluated beyond redemption? Which event formats deliver the most repeatable contribution and sponsor renewal? How do city sales, central product and content teams share ownership of an integrated offer? What is already on the roadmap that I should build on? What would you want the person in this role to have changed by day 90? "},{"title":"Interview rehearsal · Ten minutes before the interview","url":"/radio-mirchi/interview#last","text":" Remember ENIL versus Mirchi and domestic versus consolidated numbers. Review the latest initiatives; acknowledge existing work before proposing a change. Prepare two real stories: one growth result and one hard delivery / prioritisation decision. Have the event and subscriber economics models ready to explain assumptions. Use “my hypothesis” when you have not verified the problem. Finish answers with how you would measure the outcome. "},{"title":"Why me · Anchit Tandon","url":"/radio-mirchi/about#profile","text":" I am a product and growth leader with an engineering background and experience across consumer subscriptions, digital media and D2C. My approach is to connect customer needs with a measurable business outcome, then work closely with design, engineering, sales and operations to deliver it. Open my portfolio LinkedIn profile "},{"title":"Why me · Relevant experience to bring into the discussion","url":"/radio-mirchi/about#fit","text":" Experience Mirchi relevance How I would substantiate it Times Internet: ET Prime / ET Markets Subscriptions, consumer engagement, conversion and media businesses. Explain the actual customer problem, my ownership, baseline, change and measured result. VAHDAM: product and D2C growth Acquisition, lifecycle journeys, retention and commercial economics. Use verified market, period and revenue / conversion definitions. Hands-on AI and product building Fast prototypes, workflow design and implementation fluency. Demonstrate the product and explain production limits and validation. Event-related work Cross-functional planning, participant experience and execution discipline. Describe exact scope and collaborators; do not imply sole ownership of the whole event. Career context comes from Anchit’s supplied background and linked portfolio. This study does not introduce new personal performance metrics or claim ENIL insider knowledge. "},{"title":"Why me · A reliable structure for my examples","url":"/radio-mirchi/about#stories","text":" Situation: what customer or business problem existed and how it was established. Ownership: the decision I owned and the people I worked with. Action: what changed and why other options were rejected. Evidence: time period, denominator, result and how causality was assessed. Learning: what I would repeat, change or investigate next. "},{"title":"Sources & methodology · Research method and confidence","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#method","text":" Research date: 21 November 2026, India time . Financial cut-off: latest available Q2 / H1 FY27 disclosures. Source hierarchy: filed financial tables for scoped figures; management disclosures for strategy; official product pages for current propositions; public observations for experience; independent industry research for market context. Label Meaning Limit Reported Company / official source says it. Not independently audited unless explicitly stated. Observed A public browser surface was inspected in this session. Session, region, viewport and eligibility may affect behaviour. Listing evidence Store description, release notes, ratings or screenshots. Does not establish installed-app behaviour. Hypothesis / proposed Original analysis or a potential test. Not a confirmed defect or promised business result. Public browsing used a signed-out in-app browser. Desktop default was 1280 × 720. Mobile responsive checks used a 390 × 844 viewport; these are browser emulation, not a physical handset or native app test. No subscription or ticket purchase was completed, and no private account or internal company data was accessed. "},{"title":"Sources & methodology · Reconciliation and evidence cautions","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#cautions","text":" Q2 EBITDA: domestic ₹11.26 crore / +9.5%; consolidated ₹12.05 crore / +5.9%. Different scopes explain different headlines. March cash: consolidated approximately ₹423.9 crore, standalone ₹404.2 crore, distinguished in Q4 deck. The Q2 deck executive summary prints digital revenue as ₹33 million, inconsistent with its 29% share. The press release gives ₹33 crore; the domestic minus existing business bridge is approximately ₹32.93 crore. Use that cross-check. Annual narrative mix percentages and “digital as % of core radio” use different or unclear denominators. They are not combined into a precise annual pie chart. The company profile’s 38M listener claim uses IRS 2019. Latest deck reach / event-count claims vary across slides; do not add them or invent a unique audience count. Mirchi Plus store cache and live ratings differ. The live observed rating is recorded with its date rather than presented as a universal value. Featured reviews include 2019–2023 and earlier years. They are not used to claim current defect prevalence or recent sentiment. Mirchi iOS India URL was unavailable in this session; Qatar listing presence does not prove availability for India. A live event page can remain accessible after its stated campaign period. Registration availability and upcoming status are evaluated separately. "},{"title":"Sources & methodology · Source register","url":"/radio-mirchi/sources#registry","text":" Find a source S1 · 3–4 Nov 2026 ENIL Q2 FY27 investor presentation Financial tables: PDF pp. 15–17. Initiatives: pp. 19–31. Company presentation; audience claims are not independently audited. https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/stock_exchange_fillings/FY27/ENILInvestorsPresentationQ2FY27.pdf S2 · 3 Nov 2026 ENIL Q2 FY27 results press release Quarter ended 30 Sep 2026. Rounded revenue, domestic mix, digital losses and consolidated cash. https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/stock_exchange_fillings/FY27/ENILPressReleaseQ2FY27.pdf S3 · 4 Nov; filed 6 Nov 2026 ENIL Q2 FY27 earnings call transcript Management commentary, not a forecast: radio pressure, event margin discipline, acquisition costs and Gaana ambition. https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/ENIL_06112026152711_ENIL20261106TranscriptQ2FY27.pdf S4 · 18 May 2026 ENIL Q4 FY26 investor presentation FY26 consolidated table: PDF p. 19. Product updates pp. 21–25; event cases pp. 26–29. https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/stock_exchange_fillings/FY26/2026_05_18_Investor_PPT_Q4FY26.pdf S5 · FY ended 31 Mar 2026 ENIL FY26 annual report Strategy and operating review, especially printed pp. 130–133. Some narrative denominators differ from the deck; not used to reconstruct a precise annual revenue mix. https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/annual_reports/ENIL_Annual_Report_FY26.pdf S6 · 15 May 2026 ENIL Q4 FY26 results press release FY26 revenue and digital growth. The release contains two cash figures; the deck distinguishes consolidated from standalone. https://www.enil.co.in/pdf/stock_exchange_fillings/FY26/ENILPressReleaseQ426.pdf S7 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 ENIL company profile Legal entity, network and established IP catalogue. The 38M listener figure explicitly uses IRS 2019; it is historical. https://www.enil.co.in/details-of-the-business.php S8 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 ENIL management profiles Leadership context. The latest presentation is preferred when titles differ. https://www.enil.co.in/management.php S9 · 24 Mar 2026 FICCI–EY 2026 industry release Calendar-year 2025 industry estimates, not ENIL fiscal-year results. https://www.ey.com/en_in/newsroom/2026/03/india-s-media-and-entertainment-sector-grew-9-percent-to-inr-2-point-78-trillion-in-2025-driven-by-digital-and-live-experiences-ficci-ey-report S10 · 29 Oct 2026 Noise × Gaana launch announcement Official brand announcement: bundle terms and potential reach, not redeemed subscribers. https://mirchi.in/stories/music/noise-and-gaana-launch-co-branded-buds-r1-with-one-year-of-gaana-plus/156421646 S11 · 12 Oct 2026 Mirchi Navratri city guide Historical 2026 listings, dates and starting prices. Listing does not establish attendance or profit. https://mirchi.in/stories/music/navratri-2026-city-wise-guide-garba-nights-dandiya-events/156323211 S12 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Mirchi Freshers campaign website Visible registration/voting campaign; no registration submitted in this audit. https://www.mirchilive.events/ S13 · 2026 campaign Mirchi Freshers terms 100 colleges / 16 cities; campaign period stated as Aug–Sep 2026. An accessible page is not proof the contest is still accepting entries. https://www.mirchilive.events/terms S14 · 17 Nov 2026 Sunday Suspense: Indrapatan Current release announced on Mirchi Bangla YouTube and Gaana. https://mirchi.in/stories/music/mirchi-somak-stars-as-a-determined-defense-attorney-in-sunday-suspenses-legal-thriller-indrapatan/156523996 S15 · 12 Dec 2024 Mirchi Music Awards: 16th edition results Historical IP evidence. Not presented as a newly announced 2026 edition. https://mirchi.in/stories/music/16th-mirchi-music-awards-winners/151105677 S16 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Mirchi Plus Android listing Browser showed 2.9 stars, about 1.82K reviews, 1M+ downloads and 30 Mar 2024 update. Search cache showed 3.2: live observation takes precedence for this session; region/device can vary. https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.timesgroup.mirchiplay S17 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Mirchi Plus iOS listing: Qatar storefront Version 7.5 dated 1 Apr 2024. Qatar evidence cannot establish Indian availability. India URL returned page not found in browser. https://apps.apple.com/qa/app/mirchi-plus-bollywood-podcast/id1449505212 S18 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Gaana Android listing 4.2 stars, 100M+ lifetime downloads; update 4 Nov 2026 in retrieved page. Reviews displayed include old years; not a recent representative sample. https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.gaana&amp;hl=en_IN S19 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Gaana iOS India listing 4.1 stars, approximately 114K ratings; version 9.26.4 shown as two days ago. In-app purchase SKUs are not guaranteed checkout prices. https://apps.apple.com/in/app/gaana-music-songs-podcasts/id585270521 S20 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Mirchi app download landing page Mirchi Plus positioning and outbound Android / US iOS app links remain visible. https://mirchi.in/mirchi-plus-mobile-apps S21 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Mirchi Reads website Root redirected here. Gaana navigation, subscription CTAs, article categories and Gaana app QR observed. https://mirchi.in/stories S22 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Gaana web home and navigation Public browsing, app-store handoffs and social links inspected; no paid account used. https://gaana.com/ S23 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Gaana web subscription page Observed ₹1 trial, ₹709 yearly offer, ₹129 monthly and ₹899 one-time annual. Prices can vary by eligibility, platform and date. No purchase completed. https://gaana.com/subscribe/buy-gaana-plus S24 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Gaana radio discovery Public radio catalogue inspected. Category contains themed music radios; do not assume it is a city FM simulcast directory. https://gaana.com/radio S25 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Gaana podcast discovery Public discovery and Sunday Suspense destination inspected. Playback entitlement not fully tested. https://gaana.com/podcast S26 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 District: Mirchi Neon Run 2026 Listing advertises 28 Nov 2026, Chennai, 6 PM, ₹299 onwards. No ticket purchase; listing details may change. https://www.district.in/events/mirchi-neon-run-2026-nov28-2026-buy-tickets S27 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 BookMyShow: Mirchi Holicious 2026 Past event shown as closed. Useful to map distribution, not an upcoming ticket recommendation. https://in.bookmyshow.com/activities/mirchi-holicious-2026/ET00485449 S28 · 28 Aug 2024 PIB: FM expansion decision 4% annual licence fee language applies to the specified new cities. Do not apply it universally to ENIL’s existing licences. https://www.pib.gov.in/PressNoteDetails.aspx?ModuleId=3&amp;NoteId=152059&amp;lang=1&amp;reg=3 S29 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Radio City website Primary competitor surface; rendering limited in text retrieval. No current financial comparison inferred. https://www.radiocity.in/ S30 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 BIG FM website Primary competitor categories include podcasts, video, RJs and branded properties. https://www.bigfmindia.com/ S31 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Mirchi Bangla YouTube Channel presence checked; content release corroborated with S14. No deduplicated reach estimate. https://www.youtube.com/@MirchiBangla S32 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Gaana YouTube Official link discovered from Gaana footer. Social observation is separated from paid conversion. https://www.youtube.com/@Gaanaofficial S33 · Accessed 21 Nov 2026 Gaana Instagram Official footer handoff. Login walls may limit public inspection. https://www.instagram.com/gaana/ S34 · Live browser check 21 Nov 2026 Mirchi Plus Instagram Verified public profile and Noise bundle link inspected. No follower total is used as unique reach or paid audience. https://www.instagram.com/mirchiplus/ S35 · 15 Sep 2026 MIB operational private FM channel list Official station-level listing. Use city and frequency, not a national frequency assumption or a brand-wide shutdown inference. https://www.mib.gov.in/sites/default/files/2026-09/noticefm.pdf "}];